Here is the root cause:
The bug, `ConcurrentModificationException`, occurs when a collection is modified while it is being iterated over. In the context of the `getTokens()` method in `UserGroupInformation.java`, returning an unmodifiable collection directly from `getCredentialsInternal().getAllTokens()` can lead to this exception if the underlying collection is altered by another thread during iteration. By creating a new `ArrayList` to hold the tokens, the modification is avoided, thus preventing the exception.

